<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 3rd Grade (CEFR: A1.1)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> My Evening Routine</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I'm Sleepy. It's Bedtime.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: justify;" colspan="3">
                <b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Demonstrate comprehension of phrases with names and dates in a short, simple recording delivered at a slow pace. Interactive: Perform tasks based on oral instructions.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: justify;" colspan="3">
                <b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can demonstrate comprehension of familiar bedtime phrases with names and times from recordings (e.g., "It is time for bed!"). Can perform bedtime tasks from oral instructions (e.g., "It is time to brush your teeth."). Can get the main points in short conversations about bedtime (e.g., "It is time to sleep.").
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher greets students, then mimes yawning and stretching, asking, "Are you sleepy?" The teacher shows flashcards of key vocabulary (bed, pajamas, toothbrush, storybook) and asks students to point as the teacher says the word. The teacher leads a simple TPR activity: "Sleep!" (students put heads on hands), "Brush!" (students mime brushing teeth).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up flashcards one by one, clearly saying the words slowly: "bed," "pajamas," "brush," "teeth." The teacher emphasizes the pronunciation of /b/ in "bed" and /t/ in "teeth." The teacher then models simple sentences with actions: "I brush my teeth" (demonstrating), "I wear my pajamas" (pointing to self). The teacher models blending /w-ɒ-ʃ/ in "wash" and /t-iː-θ/ in "teeth."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the new vocabulary.
                    <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Holding up a toothbrush flashcard) "Is this a spoon or a toothbrush?" (Expected answer: "A toothbrush!")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Mimicking brushing hair) "Do I brush my hair or my teeth?" (Expected answer: "Your teeth!")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Evening Routine")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, simple audio recording (approx. 1 minute) of a child named Leo describing his evening routine. The register is informal and personal. The format is a brief narrative monologue.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Audio Script Example:</b> "Hi, I'm Leo. It's night time. First, I eat dinner. Then, I wash my face. Next, I brush my teeth with my toothbrush. I wear my pajamas. My mom reads a story from a book. It is time for bed! I am sleepy. Goodnight!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will demonstrate comprehension of phrases with names and routine actions delivered at a slow pace, as well as understanding of time and status expressions related to bedtime.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions (Listen for main idea):</b>
                            <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Who is talking?" (Leo)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is this story about morning or night?" (Night)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Listen for specific details):</b> The teacher will say statements based on the audio, and students respond "True" or "False."
                            <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Leo eats breakfast first." (False)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Leo's mom reads a book." (True)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Leo is tired." (True)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening for specific details and sequence in a short routine. Reinforcing grammar: sequencing words ("First, then, next, last"), present simple for routines ("I brush my teeth," "I wash my face"). Vocabulary: bed, pajamas, teeth, toothbrush, story, book, sleepy, brush, wash, sleep. Pronunciation: /b/ in "bed", /t/ in "teeth", blending /w-ɒ-ʃ/ in "wash" and /t-iː-θ/ in "teeth."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1: Listen and Point/Circle.</b> The teacher plays parts of Leo's audio routine again. Students have a worksheet with pictures of "wash face," "brush teeth," "read book," "go to bed." As they hear each action, they point to or circle the corresponding picture. The teacher repeats segments focusing on the target vocabulary.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2: Listen and Number the Sequence.</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with four mixed-up pictures representing Leo's evening routine (e.g., child washing face, child brushing teeth, mom reading a story, child in bed). The teacher plays the full audio recording of Leo's routine once more. Students number the pictures 1-4 in the correct chronological order as they hear them.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3: Listen and Follow Oral Instructions (TPR).</b> The teacher gives simple, sequential oral instructions related to bedtime using the target grammar and vocabulary. Students perform the actions.
                            <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"First, pretend to yawn because you are sleepy!"</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Then, pretend to brush your teeth." (Focus on /t/ in teeth)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Next, get into your pretend bed." (Focus on /b/ in bed)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Last, close your eyes and sleep well. Goodnight!"</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Evening Routine")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task:</b> "Listen and Draw My Bedtime Actions."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students will listen to a new set of simplified, sequential oral instructions describing a bedtime routine. Their task is to draw simple stick figures or symbols representing each action mentioned by the teacher. This focuses on interactive listening and demonstrating comprehension through a non-verbal response.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher prepares a simple drawing sheet for each student, divided into 3 or 4 boxes.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "Listen carefully. I will tell you about my evening. Draw what I do in each box."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher gives the instructions slowly, pausing after each one:
                            <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"First, I wash my face." (Students draw a face being washed)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Then, I brush my teeth." (Students draw teeth being brushed)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Next, I put on my pajamas." (Students draw pajamas)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Last, I go to bed. I am sleepy." (Students draw someone in bed)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher circulates, observing students' drawings and listening comprehension. After all instructions, students can briefly show their drawings.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation during the "Listen and Draw" activity and a simple peer-checking of drawings. The teacher uses a checklist to note students' ability to follow sequential oral instructions and recognize key vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students will hold up their drawings from Stage 4. The teacher will play a very short audio segment (e.g., "It's bedtime. First, brush your teeth. Then, go to bed.") and students point to the corresponding drawings in their sequence.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Comprehension of sequencing words (First, Then, Next, Last) demonstrated by correct order in drawings.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Recognition of core vocabulary (wash face, brush teeth, pajamas, bed) through their drawn representations.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to follow multi-step oral instructions accurately.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students will do a quick "thumbs up" or "thumbs down" response.
                    <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can I understand 'brush my teeth' when I hear it?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I understand the instructions for my drawing?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Student and Teacher Reflection)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-top: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new word you heard and understood today about bedtime?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you do when you are sleepy?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well during this listening lesson? Was the audio input appropriate for A1.1 3rd graders? Did students successfully demonstrate comprehension of the target vocabulary and sequencing words through their actions and drawings? What adjustments or scaffolds (e.g., more visuals, slower pacing, peer support) are needed for students who struggled with following multi-step oral instructions or identifying specific vocabulary for the next listening activity?</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "Great listening today, everyone! Next lesson, we will READ a short story about an evening routine using many of the same words we heard today. We will see pictures and read the words!"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>